  <event id="264">
      <start>11:45</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>H.1309</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Tasty Application Distribution with Project Bretzn</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Crossdesktop devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract></abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What makes developers and users happy? Currently developers create great software solving the user&amp;#39;s problem. But getting the software in a consumable way, simple, fast and efficient to the user nowadays still comes with some challenges. All this, and marketing of the software isn&amp;#39;t covered yet either. Enter Bretzn, a project aimed at radically simplifying the work of developers in distributing their software, enabling them to get their work to potential users by only a few clicks, directly in the tools they already use. This presentation describes both the underlying philosophies of the project, and will also show how the software works in practice through a short, live demonstration.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2641">Frank Karlitschek</person>
          <person id="2642">Dan Leinir Turthra Jensen</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>